# QuorumTrading local edition — copy to ".env" next to docker-compose.local.yml and fill in.
#
# The stack BOOTS with none of these set. CRYPTO price data (BTC, ETH, ...) is KEYLESS out of the
# box — a built-in Kraken/Coinbase feed handles crypto backfill + backtests with nothing set here.
# STOCK price data has no keyless source, so stock backfill/backtests need a market-data key below
# (a free Alpaca paper key is the easiest). Everything here is optional; set what you need.

# Postgres password (used by both the db and the backend).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=dev-password

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MARKET DATA — only needed for STOCKS (crypto is keyless, built in). Set a key to trade stocks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alpaca (US) — primary source for STOCK bars (also serves crypto, but crypto already works keyless).
# A FREE paper account gives you market-data keys; you do NOT need to fund it or enable live trading.
# The same key also powers US paper/live trading later. Sign up: https://alpaca.markets/ (API Keys).
ALPACA_API_KEY=
ALPACA_API_SECRET=

# Tiingo — no-cost fallback for daily/weekly/monthly STOCK bars (no intraday, no crypto). Handy for
# deep history. Free API token: https://www.tiingo.com/  (Account → API → Token).
TIINGO_API_TOKEN=

# Finnhub — company news for the Fundamental/Sentiment agents (not price bars). Free key:
# https://finnhub.io/
FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# Reddit — sentiment source (optional). Register a "script" app: https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CREDENTIALS ENCRYPTION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AES-256-GCM key for encrypting stored broker credentials at rest.
# STRONGLY recommended once you link a real broker. Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
BROKER_CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM ENGINE (optional — auto-detected at boot, free options first)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A local OpenAI-compatible server (Ollama :11434, LM Studio :1234, llama.cpp, vLLM) is the
# recommended keyless engine under Docker — the stack reaches it on your host via
# host.docker.internal and picks it up automatically on Ollama's default port. Only set these to
# point elsewhere or pin a model (otherwise the server's first advertised model is used):
#QT_LLM_LOCALHTTP_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
#QT_LLM_LOCALHTTP_MODEL=

# No model server but the `claude` CLI on your host? Run `npm start` in tools/claude-openai-bridge
# (serves :8088, Node, no dependencies) and point the stack at it. Not free — it spends your Claude
# subscription, and the adapter still records those calls as $0:
#QT_LLM_LOCALHTTP_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8088/v1
#QT_LLM_LOCALHTTP_MODEL=sonnet

# Other coding CLIs (codex/gemini/qwen)? Run `python3 scripts/local-llm-cli-shim.py` (serves :11435):
#QT_LLM_LOCALHTTP_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11435/v1
#QT_LLM_LOCALHTTP_MODEL=claude
# (A CLI can only be invoked DIRECTLY — without a bridge — when the backend runs natively.)

# Shared secret, if the local engine requires one. The bridge binds 127.0.0.1 and needs no key on
# Docker Desktop; on Linux you widen it with CLAUDE_BRIDGE_HOST=0.0.0.0, and then it MUST have
# CLAUDE_BRIDGE_API_KEY set to the same value you put here, or the port is open to your network.
#QT_LLM_LOCALHTTP_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter — hosted models with your own API key (also settable later, encrypted, on the
# setup page at http://localhost:8085/api/v1/llm/setup).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAXO (EU broker) — EXPERIMENTAL, largely untested. Expect rough edges.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Register a PERSONAL OAuth app at https://www.developer.saxo/ and set its redirect URI to the
# SAXO_REDIRECT_URI below, then flip SAXO_ENABLED=true. Note: Saxo's SIM (paper) environment does
# NOT serve equity/ETF market data — only Forex — so the SIM path is limited. See LOCAL_SETUP.md.
SAXO_ENABLED=false
SAXO_APP_KEY=
SAXO_APP_SECRET=
SAXO_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8085/api/v1/broker-accounts/saxo/onboard/callback
